= Discrete mathematics, probability and continuous mathematics examination paper by the University of Oxford (2013)
{parent=Computer science bibliography}
{title2=4223}
{title2=2013-06-20}

The nine-page <University of Oxford> Computer Science Prelims paper dated 20 June 2013. The public https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/past_exam_papers_for_1st_year_of/response/1398416/attach/2/Fakour%20Zip%20Final%201.zip?cookie_passthrough=1[released examination archive] contains the original scan as `4223-1.pdf`. Printed pages 2–4 cover <discrete mathematics>, pages 5–6 cover <calculus> and <ordinary differential equations>, and pages 7–9 cover <probability theory>. Question 8(c)(i) introduces the two-roll model without asking for a separate calculation; Question 8(c)(v) allows the trivial independence of an impossible <event> unless the values are restricted to the two marginal supports.

