= Discrete Mathematics, Continuous Mathematics and Probability examination paper by the University of Oxford (2014)
{c}
{parent=Computer science bibliography}
{title2=4223}
{title2=2014-06-26}

The ten-page <University of Oxford> Computer Science Prelims paper dated 26 June 2014. The public https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/past_exam_papers_for_1st_year_of/response/1398416/attach/2/Fakour%20Zip%20Final%201.zip?cookie_passthrough=1[released examination archive] contains it as `4223.pdf`. Question 1's displayed <function> requires a domain restriction. Question 3's fractional-size <recurrence relation> needs a base case and an integer-rounding convention. Question 6's parameter range includes negative values, so the critical-point classification requires a split at $\alpha=-1$ as well as $\alpha=1$; its final derivative request also has a typographical superscript on $f$. These points were checked against printed pp. 2, 4 and 7.

