= Java 8 iteration API documentation
{c}
{parent=Computer science bibliography}

Official <Java> API entries: https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/lang/Iterable.html and https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/util/Iterator.html. Locators: `Iterable.iterator()` and enhanced for support; `Iterator.hasNext()`, `Iterator.next()` exhaustion, and optional `Iterator.remove()`.

= Object Oriented Programming examination paper of the University of Oxford (2015)
{c}
{parent=Computer science bibliography}
{title2=A10400W1}
{title2=2015-06-11}

The seven-page <University of Oxford> <computer science> Finals paper dated Thursday 11 June 2015, 2:30 pm–4:00 pm. The released https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/computer_science_past_exam_paper/response/956037/attach/3/Lawrence%20Attachment.zip?cookie_passthrough=1[public examination archive] contains it as `2015-oop.pdf`. Questions 1–3 occupy printed pp. 2–7; Question 3 is explicitly marked corrected. The calendar example on p. 3 interprets its starting offset in weekday cells. The axes upper-corner expression on p. 5 has an extra closing parenthesis; its coordinatewise bounds remain readable. Figure 3 on p. 7 shows the supporting baseplate.

= OWL 2 Web Ontology Language Profiles (Second Edition)
{parent=Computer science bibliography}
{c}
{title2=11 December 2012}

https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/REC-owl2-profiles-20121211/

The profile grammar distinguishes positions where existential and universal restrictions are allowed. Section 4 supplies the <RL description logic> restrictions and Section 5 gives complexity tables. The EL profile here includes bottom and disjointness; its satisfiability result should not be confused with the trivial satisfiability of <EL> without bottom.

= Rewriting Conjunctive Queries under Description Logic Constraints
{parent=Computer science bibliography}
{c}
{title2=2008}

https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/people/ian.horrocks/Publications/download/2008/PeMH08b.pdf

Section 2 states the selection condition and Horn calculus used by <resolution with free selection>.

