The four-page <University of Oxford> Finals <computer science> examination held on 10 June 2015, Trinity Term 2015. Public primary-source archive: https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/computer_science_past_exam_paper/response/956037/attach/3/Lawrence%20Attachment.zip?cookie_passthrough=1[Lawrence Attachment.zip], member `2015-landp.pdf`. Printed p. 4, Question 3(d), permits an arbitrary <quantifier-free formula> in an asserted <least Herbrand model> equivalence; that assertion fails when negative atoms are allowed, even for a satisfiable <Horn clause>.

