{parent=Computer science bibliography}
{c}
{title2=6 January 1984}

= RFC 896
{c}
{synonym}

https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc896.html

Historical discussion of the small-packet problem and the sender rule associated with <Nagle's algorithm>.

= TCP Congestion Control (RFC 5681)
{parent=Computer science bibliography}
{c}
{title2=September 2009}

https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5681.html

Sections 2–3 define sender variables and the <TCP> <congestion control> mechanisms.

= Distance Vector Multicast Routing Protocol (RFC 1075)
{parent=Computer science bibliography}
{c}
{title2=November 1988}

https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1075.html

Historical experimental <multicast routing> specification; §2 describes reverse-path broadcasting and truncation. The examination solutions discuss the forwarding principles without treating this historical specification as a current deployment recommendation.

